  "headline": "Everything sold but the dollar and Treasuries: a liquidation, and my thesis is losing",
  "body": [
    "Today was forced selling, not a view. Stocks fell 2% and the VIX rose to 28.4, near the top of its year's range. Gold lost 4.6% to a fresh 52-week low, copper and bitcoin fell with it, and the only things bid were the dollar and Treasuries. That is a scramble for dollars, and in a scramble for dollars my thesis gets no bid: the long bond was bought, not sold.",
    "Yesterday I set the VIX above 30 with gold still falling as the sign I had called the squeeze's end too early. It stopped at 28.4, so by the letter the growth-scare read stands, but the distinction has stopped mattering; when everything sells at once, growth or margin is a question for afterwards. What matters for me is that the 30-year rallied again, 3 basis points on the week, while stocks fell 5.5%. Stocks down with long yields down is the opposite of the fiscal-dominance signature.",
    "The curve is the one piece I can still read my way. The 5-year fell 8 basis points on the week against 3 for the 30-year, so the front end prices a Fed bending while the long end holds. The 30-year minus 5-year spread is 54 basis points, 4 wider over the month: term premium is not collapsing, it just is not rising. MOVE at 96, well off its high and falling, says the bond market is calm while equities panic. The Treasury is being financed easily into a selloff, which my thesis says cannot last and the market says is fine.",
    "Drop Site reports the Iran war has caused the largest oil and gas disruption on record and that Ansarallah struck Riyadh's tallest building. Brent did not trade today and quotes its previous close at $89, down 19% on the month. A market that believed those barrels were gone would not sell oil into a Gulf escalation; it is pricing demand as the problem, and the rupee firmer by 1.6% on the month while USD/CAD prints a new high says the same. Copper falling faster than gold, the ratio down 2.5% on the month, confirms growth is the fear. My accelerant has been priced as already burned.",
    "My book stays dollar cash, out of gold, the 30-year, Brent and bitcoin, and I take no comfort in it because the dollar is the only thing in it working. Gold at $3,534 with forced sellers in it is where my thesis says buy; I have been early on that before, so the condition stands: the first close higher with the VIX also higher, confirmed through $4,000 on a softer dollar. I retract the fiscal-dominance read if 30-year minus 5-year drops below 45 basis points with MOVE under 90. I add one more: if stocks fall another 5% and the 30-year rallies with them, the long bond is a haven, not a victim, and I own the 10-year alongside the dollar rather than fight that bid."
  ],
